-- Edge strength is the Glicko-2 expected score of this consensus state against
-- the certain neutral reference. Rating supplies the verdict; RD attenuates an
-- uncertain state toward 0.5 through Glicko's own g(phi) law. There is no
-- fitted divisor and no artificial floor.
--
-- The body is laplace_edge_strength() in spi_common.h:118, already shared by
-- foundry_crawl.c:233 and explore_web.c:237. This is only the SQL entry to it,
-- added for the same reason walk_edge_weight got one: while the formula was
-- reachable from C alone, any SQL surface that wanted the foundry's notion of
-- strength had to retype the algebra -- which is precisely how
-- consensus_adjacency ended up carrying a second, hand-typed copy of the
-- Glicko-complete formula that then had nothing binding it to the engine's.
-- One body, three callers, no restatement.
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION consensus.edge_strength(p_rating bigint, p_rd bigint)
    RETURNS double precision
    AS 'MODULE_PATHNAME', 'pg_laplace_edge_strength'
    LANGUAGE C LAPLACE_IMMUTABLE_STRICT;
